WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.960
5/74-1. This is Dispatch. Receiving?

3
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.800
This is 5/74-1.

4
00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.520
-Location?
-Neukölln. close to railway station.

5
00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:47.120
Pregnancy complications.
Lipschitzallee Ecke Kölner Damm.

6
00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:48.920
On our way.

7
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.000
And could you take
the late shift tomorrow?

8
00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.800
A colleague has a family emergency.

9
00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.120
Sorry. can't do it. Next time. OK?

10
00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.760
Are you sure?
I've been phoning around for an hour.

11
00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.920
Sorry. I've also got a family emergency.

12
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.880
It's ok. I will work it out somehow.

13
00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.360
-Nothing serious. I hope?
-I have to go to Austria.

14
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.400
Austria? I didn't know
you had family there.

15
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.160
Neither did I. until recently.

16
00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:20.760
-My father died.
-Sorry to hear that.

17
00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.280
It's fine. I didn't know him.

18
00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:24.880
My biological father. I mean.

19
00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:26.960
And now I've inherited his house.

20
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.240
It's fine. we're here.

21
00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:50.760
You'll be fine.

22
00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:58.880
-Take me to hospital. Please.
-OK. let's get you to the ambulance.

23
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.280
Stop. stop. stop! The baby's coming!

24
00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:05.240
Quick. blankets!
Everything's fine. Just lie down.

25
00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.240
I can see the head.

26
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.720
Let's work together.
When I say push. push.

27
00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.080
Now push - hard.

28
00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.040
Again. with all your strength. Push!

29
00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.640
You're doing great.

30
00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.200
Another big push. Great.

31
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.400
The head's out.

32
00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.880
Take a deep breath.

33
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.080
Here she comes. She's here!

34
00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.040
Hello. little one.

35
00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:15.040
THE RED STAG INN

36
00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.840
7 HR 48 MIN 726 KM FASTEST ROUTE

37
00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:46.280
Busy night?

38
00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:02.640
Good morning baby!

39
00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.000
Morning.

40
00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:06.600
Sleep well?

41
00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.560
Well enough.

42
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.720
I've packed everything
except your toilet stuff.

43
00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.520
Nervous?

44
00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:26.560
We don't have to go there.
We could fix all the stuff from here.

45
00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.720
No. we're definitely going.

46
00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.400
- Did you water the plants?
- Yes.

47
00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.720
- Are all the windows closed?
- Yes.

48
00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.920
Are you sure this is the right place?

49
00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.040
They cancelled the booking.

50
00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:13.640
Seriously!

51
00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.400
This is shit.

52
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:21.920
What now?

53
00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.160
No idea.

54
00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.040
Let's just go to the house.

55
00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:29.720
Maybe that woman who's taking
care of everything is there.

56
00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:30.360
Your destination is on the left.

57
00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:09.720
Holy shit.

58
00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.840
SURGERY DR. EDUARD SARSTEINER
GENERAL PRACTITIONER

59
00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.120
Judith?

60
00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:44.400
Yes?

61
00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.560
You won't remember me. I'm Paula.

62
00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:55.920
You can call me Auntie Paula.
just like you used to.

63
00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:01.840
Welcome home. Judith.

64
00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:12.400
I'm Ryan.

65
00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:15.680
- Judith's husband.
- Hello. Ryan.

66
00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.800
Come on in. Moni! They're here!

67
00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:25.520
We have prepared a room for you.
I hope that's fine.

68
00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:28.920
That's fine.

69
00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.960
- Right?
- Yes.

70
00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:39.080
Hello! We can keep it informal. right?

71
00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.600
After all.
I knew you when you were this big.

72
00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.680
This is Monika. Ms. Ramsauer.
She's been helping out.

73
00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.800
It's so nice that you're back.

74
00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:50.400
Even if it is a sad occasion.

75
00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:53.920
Anyway. never mind.
I'll let you settle in.

76
00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.520
Let me know if you need
help with anything.

77
00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:59.280
And that goes for you two. too. Bye.

78
00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.880
Yes. and there's some food in the oven.

79
00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:08.000
I made something vegetarian.
Can't be too careful these days.

80
00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:11.280
Come on. I'll show you to your room.

81
00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.640
How was the trip?
Did everything go smoothly?

82
00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:17.360
Yes. it was fine.

83
00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:20.800
Do you want to see the house now.
or shall we wait for daylight?

84
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.400
Tomorrow will be fine. The real
estate agent isn't coming until noon.

85
00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.000
Eduard. your father...

86
00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.600
He would certainly have wanted
the house to stay in the family.

87
00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.200
Then he should have taken
care of his daughter.

88
00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:41.080
You keep talking about my father.
There's no mother?

89
00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.480
Just get settled in.
You must be tired after the long drive.

90
00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:46.680
Maybe she's still running
around this dump somewhere.

91
00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:47.920
Judith. she's dead.

92
00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:50.960
She died a long time ago.

93
00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:58.840
I'm sure you have a lot of questions
and I will try to answer them for you.

94
00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.080
When the time is right.

95
00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:05.680
Reception is terrible here.
but there is a landline

96
00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.720
and my number's on the kitchen table.

97
00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:13.840
This place...

98
00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.440
Keeps going.

99
00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.040
Thanks!

100
00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.080
Cheers.

101
00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:22.520
Is that your father?

102
00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:24.840
Maybe.

103
00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:30.320
Interesting guy.

104
00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.200
I mean...

105
00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.440
Who were these people?

106
00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:38.480
They live in a house like this.
then abandon their only child?

107
00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:41.640
Money can't have been an issue.

108
00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:53.000
I always thought my mother might
have been a junkie... or a minor.

109
00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.760
That she had to give me up.

110
00:16:57.560 --> 00:16:58.800
Would you have preferred that?

111
00:16:59.440 --> 00:17:01.320
It would make it easier.

112
00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:06.440
Is everything OK?

113
00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.120
Yes.

114
00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:16.080
How much do you think this
place is worth? Altogether?

115
00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:20.720
I don't know. It needs a lot of work.

116
00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:25.160
And the area is hardly booming.

117
00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:27.760
You won't get rich.

118
00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.760
- But I love you anyway.
- Thanks.

119
00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.040
Do you actually have to accept
an inheritance?

120
00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.120
No idea.

121
00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:44.920
But there are no debts.
so you would make some money.

122
00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.680
And what would you do with all that money?

123
00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.040
I'm happy when you're happy.

124
00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:18.040
- Morning. Baby.
- Morning.

125
00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:21.400
Your room?

126
00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:24.000
No idea.

127
00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:28.440
Sleep well?

128
00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.120
Yes... Like a stone.

129
00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:39.840
- What are those pills?
- Antidepressants and antipsychotics.

130
00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:42.200
Are they taken together?

131
00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:46.080
For some mental health conditions.
Schizophrenia. for example.

132
00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:55.280
I can develop this in Berlin.

133
00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:04.280
Good morning. Sorry to disturb you.
Doctor. It's an emergency.

134
00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:06.040
You are a doctor?

135
00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:08.760
Yes. I am.
But can't you call an ambulance?

136
00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:11.680
No. The nearest hospital is an hour away.

137
00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:13.840
My mother has chronic pain.

138
00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:15.520
What is she taking?

139
00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:19.920
Oxycodone. Your father has some
in the medicine cabinet.

140
00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:25.160
- How long has she been taking it?
- I wouldn't be here if it wasn't urgent.

141
00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:29.520
Hold on a moment. yeah?

142
00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:35.240
What's up?

143
00:22:35.800 --> 00:22:37.560
I have to go out. It's an Emergency.

144
00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:39.160
Emergency?

145
00:22:39.320 --> 00:22:40.920
Yes. an emergency.

146
00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:43.320
The real estate agent arrives at eleven.
Can you get the photos done by then?

147
00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:44.440
Yes. sure.

148
00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:24.240
Thank you for coming.
My name is Franz Scheichl.

149
00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:28.360
Your father always looked after my mother.

150
00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:31.040
Without him. she'd be long gone.

151
00:23:32.840 --> 00:23:34.520
What was my father like?

152
00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:37.000
A great doctor.

153
00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:39.520
And a good hunter.

154
00:23:42.640 --> 00:23:44.000
That's it?

155
00:24:15.840 --> 00:24:16.960
Mum?

156
00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:24.600
Mum. the doctor's here.

157
00:24:39.040 --> 00:24:42.600
Mrs. Scheichl? I'll just give you
a quick examination. alright?

158
00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:18.320
Judith?

159
00:25:42.520 --> 00:25:44.440
I'm scared.

160
00:25:45.680 --> 00:25:47.640
You don't have to be scared.

161
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:50.560
What's it like over there?

162
00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:53.520
On the other side?

163
00:25:57.120 --> 00:26:00.160
You've been there.

164
00:26:13.560 --> 00:26:15.160
What did your mother mean?

165
00:26:20.200 --> 00:26:21.720
She often talks nonsense.

166
00:26:22.600 --> 00:26:24.240
Especially when she's in pain.

167
00:26:25.440 --> 00:26:26.720
Did you actually know me?

168
00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:30.560
As a child. I mean.

169
00:26:31.720 --> 00:26:32.960
Yes. I did.

170
00:26:33.120 --> 00:26:35.400
And? What was I like?

171
00:26:35.560 --> 00:26:39.920
Just a child. You ran around.
you played. you cried. That's it.

172
00:26:40.720 --> 00:26:42.400
Why did my parents give me up?

173
00:26:46.240 --> 00:26:47.840
You just disappeared one day.

174
00:26:50.720 --> 00:26:53.520
And my mother?
Did she also just "disappear"?

175
00:26:58.400 --> 00:26:59.320
Yes.

176
00:26:59.960 --> 00:27:03.760
-Did no one find that strange?
-Look. people talk a lot of crap.

177
00:27:03.920 --> 00:27:05.800
I helped you. so now it's your turn.

178
00:27:05.960 --> 00:27:08.960
People say that. out here. everybody
knows everybody else's business.

179
00:27:09.120 --> 00:27:10.320
But that's not true.

180
00:27:11.720 --> 00:27:12.640
Who is this?

181
00:27:20.200 --> 00:27:21.440
Hanna Schatzenberger.

182
00:27:22.560 --> 00:27:24.760
She was a friend of your mother's.

183
00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:26.840
Where can I find her?

184
00:27:27.560 --> 00:27:29.240
I'll give you the address.

185
00:27:31.640 --> 00:27:33.680
It's some way out of town.

186
00:28:00.320 --> 00:28:02.440
What the...

187
00:28:23.440 --> 00:28:27.120
- Sorry. I didn't mean to scare you.
- It's fine.

188
00:28:27.280 --> 00:28:29.320
Here's a little welcome present.

189
00:28:29.480 --> 00:28:32.240
Thanks. that wouldn't have been necessary.

190
00:28:33.280 --> 00:28:34.800
May I take a look?

191
00:28:40.440 --> 00:28:41.960
These pictures aren't great.

192
00:28:43.120 --> 00:28:44.840
I don't know what happened.

193
00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:47.760
Well. you're a professional.
You'll sort it out.

194
00:28:49.600 --> 00:28:50.600
Sure.

195
00:28:50.760 --> 00:28:53.960
Maybe the house just doesn't
want to be photographed.

196
00:28:56.720 --> 00:29:00.080
Do you actually enjoy it?
Shooting weddings?

197
00:29:00.240 --> 00:29:02.640
You used to work in advertising.
didn't you?

198
00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:05.160
Until the work dried up.

199
00:29:06.120 --> 00:29:07.040
Right?

200
00:29:07.840 --> 00:29:11.560
May I be a little indiscreet?
How long have you been married?

201
00:29:12.680 --> 00:29:15.480
- Three years.
- And where did you meet?

202
00:29:16.840 --> 00:29:17.840
At the cinema.

203
00:29:19.000 --> 00:29:20.760
During French Film Week.

204
00:29:22.240 --> 00:29:23.600
Both Francophiles.

205
00:29:24.680 --> 00:29:26.120
Oui. oui. la la.

206
00:29:27.600 --> 00:29:31.240
And how is the family planning going?
I mean. nobody is getting any younger.

207
00:29:33.240 --> 00:29:34.560
No plans at all.

208
00:29:35.440 --> 00:29:37.360
You could make a fresh start here.

209
00:29:37.520 --> 00:29:38.920
There are lots of weddings
out here in the countryside

210
00:29:39.080 --> 00:29:40.400
and it's a great place for children.

211
00:29:40.560 --> 00:29:41.960
What's that African saying?

212
00:29:43.280 --> 00:29:45.960
"It takes a village to raise a child."

213
00:33:40.240 --> 00:33:43.160
I'm really embarrassed.
I don't usually get lost.

214
00:33:43.920 --> 00:33:45.760
It's very easy to do here.

215
00:33:47.080 --> 00:33:48.280
But why are you soaked?

216
00:33:49.720 --> 00:33:51.960
I stumbled on the shore
and ended up in the lake.

217
00:33:53.120 --> 00:33:54.560
It's nice to have you back. Doctor.

218
00:33:56.680 --> 00:33:58.720
I'm Susi Loidl.

219
00:33:58.880 --> 00:34:00.160
Another aunt?

220
00:34:00.760 --> 00:34:02.920
Practically.
I own the dog grooming service here.

221
00:34:04.920 --> 00:34:06.560
You look great.

222
00:34:07.120 --> 00:34:08.920
You're going to stay here with us. right?

223
00:34:10.200 --> 00:34:11.960
It's such a wonderful place for children.

224
00:34:12.120 --> 00:34:14.200
Wouldn't it be great if there
was a child here again?

225
00:34:15.280 --> 00:34:16.520
We are perfectly happy without children.

226
00:34:17.960 --> 00:34:20.400
A lovely woman like you without children?

227
00:34:20.560 --> 00:34:23.880
- We can't have that!
- I like my life just fine the way it is.

228
00:34:24.040 --> 00:34:26.840
You've still got time...
A little. at least.

229
00:34:27.600 --> 00:34:29.360
- Right. Susi?
- Right.

230
00:34:50.040 --> 00:34:50.960
Thank you.

231
00:34:51.520 --> 00:34:52.520
See you next week.

232
00:34:53.920 --> 00:34:55.880
- What's happening next week?
- I have an appointment.

233
00:34:56.400 --> 00:35:00.280
- At your doctor's office.
- Yes. me too... A check-up.

234
00:35:01.760 --> 00:35:04.160
- We'll be back in Berlin next week.
- Dear.

235
00:35:04.960 --> 00:35:06.400
We'll see.

236
00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:08.560
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye. Doctor.

237
00:35:33.080 --> 00:35:34.440
Ryan!

238
00:35:45.320 --> 00:35:46.640
Ryan!

239
00:36:24.600 --> 00:36:25.960
Ryan!

240
00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:13.520
Don't open the door!

241
00:37:14.720 --> 00:37:15.960
What are you doing down there?

242
00:37:16.120 --> 00:37:17.640
Wait. One second.

243
00:37:20.200 --> 00:37:23.360
Sorry. baby. I was developing negatives.

244
00:37:24.360 --> 00:37:26.560
- What took you so long?
- I got lost.

245
00:37:26.720 --> 00:37:29.040
- You did?
- Yeah. me.

246
00:37:34.440 --> 00:37:36.080
Something's wrong with my camera.

247
00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:38.480
Then I found this one...

248
00:37:40.600 --> 00:37:42.280
A fucking Nikon F4.

249
00:37:43.560 --> 00:37:45.600
The darkroom still works.

250
00:37:47.360 --> 00:37:49.080
Even the chemicals are fine.

251
00:37:50.480 --> 00:37:51.920
I can develop the images here.

252
00:38:00.280 --> 00:38:01.720
Do you think that's her?

253
00:38:04.960 --> 00:38:07.760
I always wanted to get to know my mother.

254
00:38:11.600 --> 00:38:13.080
I'll finish up here.

255
00:38:13.240 --> 00:38:15.480
And then you'll finally
get to know her. OK?

256
00:38:20.800 --> 00:38:22.120
I'm going to have a bath first.

257
00:38:22.280 --> 00:38:24.040
By the way. the realtor was here.

258
00:38:25.120 --> 00:38:26.360
Shit. sorry.

259
00:38:28.240 --> 00:38:29.640
She'll come back tomorrow.

260
00:41:32.880 --> 00:41:33.800
Judith!

261
00:41:35.080 --> 00:41:36.120
Judith?

262
00:41:36.960 --> 00:41:38.800
Hey. hey. hey.

263
00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:44.240
Komm. Hey. hey.

264
00:42:05.320 --> 00:42:07.000
It felt so real.

265
